WEBVTT

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.340
I wish Mom could be here, too.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.650
Oh, well. It’s our fault for making plans on the same day
she’d set aside for a karaoke tournament.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.250
Go, you’re awfully quiet.
Are you carsick?

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.210
Go.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.300
Are you all right?

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.380
She asked you if you were carsick.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.950
Me? I’m totally fine.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.970
Are <i>you</i> okay, though?

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.210
You were working late again
last night, yeah?

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.150
We worked hard
so we could enjoy this day!

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.850
Couldn’t be better!

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.690
That’s great to hear!

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.600
By the way, why did you decide
to go to Hiwada Town again?

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.240
We couldn’t really enjoy our last trip
because of the pouring rain, remember?

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.210
So we talked it out and decided...

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.720
...that this time, we <i>will</i> create
some happy memories!

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.950
I see. Thanks!

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.690
PocketMonsters

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.190
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.940
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.440
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.160
And skip the slow send-off

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.530
Be it through fire or through water

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.240
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.170
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:52.340
Each and every one of my memories

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:57.130
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.140
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:07.730
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:13.150
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:17.450
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.700
Let's have a fight!

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.410
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.620
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:28.870
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:34.380
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.630
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.180
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.430
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.100
I choose you!

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:57.110
Celebi — A Timeless Promise

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:57.120
Hiwada Town, Johto Region
Celebi — A Timeless Promise

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:57.890
Hiwada Town, Johto Region

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.640
Go went on
a family vacation...
Hiwada Town, Johto Region

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.120
...to Hiwada Town
in the Johto Region.
Hiwada Town, Johto Region

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.910
It’s your turn, Kimawari.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.670
Good day, Sir.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.780
Thank you for having us.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.040
You’re quite welcome.
It’s been far too long.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.800
It’s been... A year? No, two?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.680
Three years!

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.000
Oh! The little boy from back then!

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.670
Wasn’t your name...

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:31.500
I’m Go!

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.050
That’s it! You sure have grown!

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.260
He’s ten already.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.140
He’s even become a Pokémon Trainer!

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.720
I suppose these two
are your partners, then?

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.930
Yes! These are
Rabbifoot and Messon.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:43.820
I see.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.490
It disappeared!

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.290
Long time, no see, Kimawari.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:54.710
I’ve grown, yeah?

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.490
Here’s the cottage key.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:59.200
When you check out...

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.650
Leave it in the mailbox, right?

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.680
All right, enjoy yourselves!

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:12.880
Nothing beats the view here!

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.450
The air is so fresh,
and it’s so quiet!

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.550
We can really relax here!

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:22.570
So, what do you wanna do now?

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.320
And they’re already asleep...

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.720
They look comfortable.
They must have been really tired.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.040
Shall we go catch some
Johto Pokémon, then?

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:44.490
What Pokémon live around here...?

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:58.630
I can’t believe Mom and Dad
fell asleep the moment we got here!

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:02.600
What do they expect me to do for fun
all on my own in the middle of the mountains?!

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.160
A Hoho!

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:17.880
Awesome!

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.840
There’s so many Pokémon!

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.790
Maybe Mew will be here, too!

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.180
All right! I’m gonna find Mew!

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:39.730
Mew! Come out
if you’re there! Mew!

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.600
I guess it won’t be that easy to find.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.560
It <i>is</i> a Mythical Pokémon, after all!

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.120
Mew?!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.250
Wait, Mew!

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:05.800
Wait!

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:06.740
Mew!

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.180
Celebi!

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:15.670
Ow....

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:17.670
And you are?!

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:18.840
What about you?

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.180
It was just a Muma?

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.850
Oh...

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.320
You were just shouting
“Celebi,” weren’t you?

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.200
And you said “Mew.”

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.160
What a screwup! How could you
mistake Muma for Celebi?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.860
You’re one to talk!

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.330
You thought it was a Mew!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.590
Well... I guess so...

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:46.100
So we’re in the same boat.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:49.080
Okay, I guess we’ll leave it at that.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.720
I’m Tokio from Tamba City.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.060
I’m Go from Kuchiba City.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.650
Nice to meet you!

00:06:58.650 --> 00:06:59.670
Same to you!

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.050
So you’re looking for Mew?

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.200
Yeah. Awesome, huh?

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.320
I don’t know...

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.180
Seriously? It’s <i>Mew</i>, you know!

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:11.780
But you’re just <i>searching</i> for it, right?
So you’re no different from me.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.100
Hang on!
Don’t get too shocked by this, but...

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.770
I’ve <i>seen</i> Mew!

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:18.120
What? For real?!

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.440
Yeah!

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.440
You know Professor Okido, yeah?

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.510
Of course!
The famous Pokémon Professor, right?

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.300
One time, at his Pokémon Camp...

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.470
I saw Mew!

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.370
That’s incredible!

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:35.370
It’s said to live deep in the jungle...

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:39.750
But it’s capable of making itself invisible at will,
so it’s very hard to spot.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.670
But you still got to meet it...
You’re so lucky!

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:45.820
And you know what else?

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:49.720
Mew is said to possess the genes
of all Pokémon.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.260
Yeah, I know.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.180
But you know a lot
about Pokémon!

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:57.810
Sure do! I’ll tell you
whatever you want to know!

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.860
Well, then,
what do you know about Celebi?

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:05.320
I know plenty,
but let’s hear what <i>you</i> know first.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:08.990
Celebi is revered
as a god of the forest.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.380
It appears wherever beautiful forests exist.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.200
Yeah, that’s right!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.680
But the most incredible thing
about it is its time travel ability!

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.260
Time travel?

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:24.730
It can travel through time,
and apparently it came from the future.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:29.570
That's why they say that so long as Celebi appears,
a bright and shining future awaits us.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.510
I see! But, you know...

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.700
I got this bright and shining
future right here in my hands!

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.690
Don’t make me say it again.
It’s embarrassing.

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:42.150
Sorry.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:43.360
But I envy you.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.900
You’re confident enough
to grasp the future in the palm of your hand!

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.250
You think?

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:52.970
I actually just got that line
from a song Dad was listening to, though...

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:56.330
Nobody can beat me
in confidence!

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:59.120
Even I couldn’t
tell you <i>why,</i> though.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:03.510
So, have you ever met Celebi?

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:06.400
Um... No, not even once.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.770
I see.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.770
I’ll help you look, then.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.970
What? Are you sure?

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.990
Aren’t you searching for Mew?

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.560
It’s fine!
I’d like to meet Celebi, too.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:20.060
Really? Okay,
let’s look together, then!

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.100
Yeah!

00:09:57.350 --> 00:10:00.220
I suppose we won’t find it that easily.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.830
That must be why they call it
a Mythical Pokémon.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.530
Yeah.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:06.900
But don’t give up yet.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:08.860
In times like these...

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:11.420
Ta-daah!

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.910
What’s that?

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:16.990
A machine to gather info on Mew
from all over the world!

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:19.700
I thought maybe we can find
things on Celebi with it, too.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.400
Did you make it?

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.260
No, my mom and dad did.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.520
Your mom and dad are amazing!

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.710
I know, right?

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:30.090
First I just had a desktop computer,

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:33.180
but they made this so I could use it
when I was outside, too.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.050
I see.

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:36.430
Oh! There <i>are</i> reported sightings of it!

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:37.180
Really?

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:41.480
Let’s see...
There’s an old shrine in Ubame Forest,

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.690
and they saw Celebi next to it.

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:45.060
Ubame Forest?

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.730
Let me check my map.

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:49.170
Got it.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:52.420
We just gotta go through the cave
behind that waterfall!

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:55.240
What do we do?

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.570
What else? Let’s go!

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:05.750
This is Ubame Forest?

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.600
I can’t tell where we’d find a shrine!

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.290
In that case...

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.400
In that case...?

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.060
We just gotta go!

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.070
Outta my way!

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:19.490
All right!
I’m coming with you!

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.240
An Ariados!

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:28.150
Run!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.280
It’s not coming after us.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:36.750
All right! One more try!

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.630
I won’t lose!

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.890
Now a Kunugidama!

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:49.630
There’s probably lots more
where that came from...

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:51.640
Definitely.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:53.170
What do we do?

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:55.550
I know!

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:57.470
Wait here for me, Tokio!

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:59.030
Huh? Where are you going?

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.110
I’ll be right back!

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:05.350
PocketMonsters

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:06.980
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:11.540
PocketMonsters

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:16.460
Grass
Kimawari
PocketMonsters

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:22.850
Hey!

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.710
A Kimawari?
Where’d you get that?

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:30.950
I borrowed it from the janitor
at the cottage I’m staying in.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:34.540
Kimawari’s Razor Leaf
can cut down that tall grass, yeah?

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:36.230
I see...

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:37.860
What a relief!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.430
Huh? What?

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:43.950
I wasn’t sure what I’d do
if you didn’t come back!

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.810
I said I’d be right back!

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:49.760
You weren’t, though!
You really kept me waiting!

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:51.500
Sorry!

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:55.280
But I never break my promises!

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.020
That’s just not who I am!

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:00.010
Me, too!
I always keep my promises!

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:02.380
Okay! Resume search!

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.010
Resume search!

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.890
Kimawari! Razor Leaf!

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:10.440
Good, keep it up!

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.890
Another Razor Leaf!

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.680
See the shrine?

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:20.030
No.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:21.630
Let’s look further in.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:22.990
Kimawari, it’s your turn.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:28.570
It’s a Kireihana!

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:29.740
It’s so cute!

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.300
Never give up!

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:38.000
Of course!

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:43.480
Nothing here. You see it?

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.870
No.

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:47.800
Kimawari,
we’re going deeper!

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.570
It’s so beautiful.

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:07.720
Yeah.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.280
I just remembered,
when the sun sets, Kimawari...

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.160
...comes to a complete stop,
doesn’t it?

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.850
Guess this is as far as we go...

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.460
We should take a break, too.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.420
It’s the first star!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:33.460
We’ll probably get to see
lots of stars here.

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:39.610
Yeah. When I look at all the stars,
it reminds me how vast the universe is.

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:42.060
The universe, huh...?

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:47.120
People spread rumors that Starmie
may be an invader from outer space.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:52.070
And that it uses the seven-colored core of its body
to send electric waves into outer space.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.440
And the moon reminds me of...

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:54.740
Pippi!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.880
On nights with a full moon,
they gather together and dance.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:59.110
And they evolve
with the Moon Stone.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.590
A shooting star!

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:03.710
Shooting stars remind me of Pi.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:09.970
Because of its unusual, starlike silhouette,
people believe that it came here on a meteor.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.640
Oh, I forgot a real great one!

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:16.790
Space really reminds you
of Rayquaza, yeah?

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.000
That one’s really cool.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.400
But I think more of Jirachi.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:24.250
Once every 1,000 years, the light of a comet
and a pure singing voice will rouse it...

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:28.970
...from its near-perpetual slumber.
It wakes for only seven days.

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:33.180
What’s wrong?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.410
I’m getting kinda cold.

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:38.350
Guess we’d better head back, then.

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:39.170
Yeah.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.800
I’m sorry about this.
Isn’t it heavy?

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:46.290
Piece of cake!

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:48.530
We’re going this way. You?

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:49.840
I’m heading that way.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.410
Let’s meet up again
in Ubame Forest tomorrow!

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.470
Really? I’d love to!

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:55.600
See ya!

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:57.350
Go!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.480
It’s a promise!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.480
Of course!
We’re friends, yeah?

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.860
Yeah! Friends!

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.290
Tomorrow!

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.250
See ya later!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:29.560
Did he oversleep?

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:47.130
I even brought hot cocoa
and stew with star-shaped carrots...

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:54.400
You said it was a promise...

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.150
You said we were friends...

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:07.920
Tokio, you jerk!

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:19.450
You’re completely drenched!
What happened?

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:20.680
Where’s your friend?

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:26.890
That was our
first and last meeting.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.690
And that’s why I...

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:37.350
Of course.
I’ve got you guys.

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:40.700
All right! Let’s get ourselves
loads of Johto Pokémon!

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:45.370
You guys help me, too!

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:50.890
Cut down the grass
so we can get into the forest!

00:17:50.890 --> 00:17:52.260
Strike, use Slash!

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:53.920
And Kamonegi, use Cut!

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.480
Knew I could count on
my Pokémon!

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.390
Keep going! Slash!

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:07.480
Run!

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:12.660
Go, Monster Ball!

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:22.700
Ariados’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:29.710
Go!

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:40.140
Kunugidama’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:45.640
Why do I keep thinking of <i>him?</i>

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:51.150
He’s... not my friend anymore!

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:08.830
The shrine!

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:13.180
I’m pretty sure Celebi showed up
near the shrine...

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:29.600
“Go, I’m sorry I broke our promise.”

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:30.600
Huh?

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:32.980
Tokio...

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:37.280
You might not believe me
at this point,

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:41.040
but I really did try to go to
Ubame Forest on that day.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:43.250
But I caught a fever...

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:47.000
I tried to go back the day after, but...

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:50.870
Go!

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:53.880
I’m sorry.

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:56.130
I know I said I promised.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:59.060
I know I said we were friends.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:07.530
I went looking for the shrine again
the next year.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.390
And I finally found it.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.280
Celebi!

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:22.280
If I could meet Celebi,
I was going to ask it...

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:28.630
...to use its time power to send me back to that day
one year earlier so I could keep my promise to you.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:30.790
But...

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:37.890
That’s why I’m
writing you this letter.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:41.970
I just wanted to let you know.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:51.470
I still think of you as my friend.

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:55.350
Tokio...

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:02.800
Go?!

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.140
Tokio?

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:27.350
There’s so much
I want to tell you.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.060
Pocket Monsters...

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:34.060
Pokémon for short.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:37.040
The strange, strange creatures
who live on this planet.

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:38.800
You can find them
all over the world,

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:41.340
forming many different
kinds of bonds.

